# Dart enum shorthand

When the expected type is already an enum, write `.member` instead of `EnumName.member`.

Applies to arguments, return values, assignments with an explicit enum type, switch cases, and enum statics such as `.values`.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
apply(Flavor.dev);
final Flavor flavor = Flavor.stage;
switch (flavor) {
  Flavor.dev => 'dev',
  Flavor.stage => 'stage',
  Flavor.prod => 'prod',
}
localStoreEngine: LocalStoreEngine.values.byName(raw),

// ✅ GOOD
apply(.dev);
final Flavor flavor = .stage;
switch (flavor) {
  .dev => 'dev',
  .stage => 'stage',
  .prod => 'prod',
}
localStoreEngine: .values.byName(raw),
```

Notes:

- Keep `EnumName.member` when there is no type context (`final flavor = Flavor.dev`).
- Do not rewrite generated files (`*.g.dart`, `*.gen.dart`, `*.freezed.dart`) to apply this.
